      "side": 0,
      "message": "The condition ‘cpi-\u003erc.frames_to_key \u003e 1’ breaks the original intent of enabling smooth_intra mode for key frames. ‘cpi-\u003erc.frames_to_key’ represents the number of frames remaining until the next key frame. For the first key frame, this value is typically greater than 1 in good encoding mode. As a result, ‘sf-\u003eintra_sf.disable_smooth_intra’ will be set to 1 for all the frames.\n\nWe also experimented with always enabling smooth_intra for speed levels 5 and 6 (i.e., setting sf.disable_smooth_intra \u003d 0 for all frames), similar to the current change in this CL for speeds 2, 3, and 4. However, for speeds 5 and 6, the results were not within an acceptable trade-off, as the encoder speed loss was higher.\n\nTherefore, we have kept the existing configuration for speeds 5 and 6 by setting disable_smooth_intra \u003d 1 in Patch-set 3 (this fixes the issue). This will result in a bit-exact change for speed 5 and 6.\n\nBelow are the results for disabling sf ‘disable_smooth_intra’ for all the frames.\n\n```\n                 Encoder Instruction                     BD-Rate Loss(%)\ncpu   Resolution  Count Reduction(%)   avg.psnr  ovr.psnr   ssim      vmaf    vmaf_neg\n 2       LOWRES2       -0.876          -0.0812   -0.0908   -0.1404   -0.2234   -0.1509\n 2       MIDRES2       -1.560          -0.1750   -0.1689   -0.1839   -0.2668   -0.2011\n 2    SHORTS608p       -2.036          -0.1662   -0.1407   -0.1745   -0.2678   -0.1806\n 2    SHORTS720p       -2.451          -0.1893   -0.1816   -0.206    -0.2789   -0.2078\n 2   SHORTS1080p       -1.959          -0.2820   -0.2690   -0.3401   -0.3144   -0.2873\n 2        HDRES2       -0.994          -0.2631   -0.2742   -0.2786   -0.3711   -0.3513\n 2       Average       -1.692          -0.1946   -0.1884   -0.2224   -0.2871   -0.2294\n\n 3       LOWRES2       -0.832          -0.0585   -0.0710   -0.0763   -0.0736   -0.0881\n 3       MIDRES2       -0.618          -0.1565   -0.1372   -0.2540   -0.2670 